<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea says to seek 40,000 tonnes of soybean.</title>
<headline>S.Korea says to seek 40,000 tonnes of soybean.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's state-run Agricultural and Fishery Marketing Corp (AFMC) said on Wednesday it would invite a tender to buy 40,000 tonnes of No.1 soybean on May 16.</p>
<p>An official at the corporation said it would close the bids by 4:00 p.m. (0700 GMT) on May 15.</p>
<p>Details for the tender are as follows:</p>
<p>POSITION  TONNE	     SHIPMENT		ARRIVAL/PORT</p>
<p>			 U.S. GULF	U.S. PNW</p>
<p>  ONE     20,000   May 26-Jun 15  Jun 11-30   Jul 20/Inchon</p>
<p>  TWO     20,000   Jun 26-Jul 15  Jul 11-30   Aug 20/Inchon</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
